Part 1 · Your Mission
Build Something Real
Your goal is to create a complete AI application that solves a real problem. Think beyond just a "demo" or a simple script aim for something a user would actually pay for!
What is RocketRide?
Think of RocketRide as a smart workspace (or "meta-harness") for AI. It helps you connect different AI models together into a pipeline which is just a sequence of steps that process data automatically.
Why use RocketRide?
Save Time: We handle the infrastructure so you can focus on your code.
Scale Easily: Move from one test to thousands of files without breaking a sweat.
Collaborate: Work with your team on shared AI workflows in the cloud.
How to Win: Make it "Load-Bearing"
A "load-bearing" app is one where RocketRide is doing the heavy lifting. Don't just make one AI call; build a system that uses these features:
Batch Processing: Handle thousands of records at once.
Mixed Media: Use text, images, and audio in one single flow.
Multi-Agent: Use "specialist" AIs that check each other's work.
What a Winning Submission Looks Like
A Specific User: Solve a problem for a specific group, like "student study planners."
Automatic Work: Input should arrive via uploads or feeds, not just copy-pasting.
Real-World Action: The app should send an email, file a ticket, or update a database.
Human-in-the-loop: The AI should ask a person for help if it isn't confident.
Judging Criteria
We are looking for apps that are publishable, solve a real problem, and handle errors gracefully. Avoid submissions that only work on a few samples or don't have a human oversight step.
What we are judging



What wins
Is it a real app?
Publishable. A stranger could sign up and get value without you explaining it.
Would someone pay?
A named user with a named problem, not a category.
Is RocketRide the engine?
Pipelines do the work. Not one model call behind a landing page.
Does it hold up at volume?
We hand it a batch, not a demo input. It holds, and the cost is sane.
Does it know when to stop?
A validator, a confidence line, a human gate.
Would it still run next month?
Malformed input, provider timeouts, a predictable cost per run.


Disqualifies: works on three sample inputs only · no path to a human anywhere · no idea what it costs per run · a single model call with a landing page.


