The canvas
Watch this first, it takes a minute:

https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rocketride-org/rocketride-server/develop/images/first_pipe.gif
Make a new file ending in .pipe and it opens straight into the canvas. You get Select your starting point: Chat to type at it, Dropper to drop files in, Web Hook for something else calling you. It also offers templates that already run, including RAG Chat and Document Parser. Starting from a template and deleting what you do not need is usually faster than building from scratch.
Drag nodes on, connect the sockets, hit Play. A red gear means a node is not configured, usually a missing API key. While it runs you get live traces: execution path, token usage, memory stats. That is where you look when something misbehaves, because it shows you which node stopped rather than making you guess.
Build one node at a time and run after each addition. Wiring five nodes and then debugging is far slower.

3. The one concept worth understanding
There are two kinds of wire on the canvas and they mean different things. This trips up everybody once.



Data lanes
